      "id": "s02",
      "type": "TITLE_CARD",
      "narration": "React is a JavaScript library for building user interfaces, one small piece at a time.",
      "durationFrames": 216,
      "timingSource": "estimated",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "transition": "wipe",
      "data": {
        "title": "React Basics",
        "subtitle": "a UI, piece by piece"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s03",
      "type": "KINETIC_TEXT",
      "narration": "The one big idea behind all of React: build your interface out of components.",
      "durationFrames": 198,
      "timingSource": "estimated",
      "background": "zoneB",
      "transition": "fade",
      "data": {
        "kinetic": {"fx": "typewriter", "text": "Build UIs from components.", "sub": "the one big idea", "color": "blue", "atWord": 9}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s04",
      "type": "DIAGRAM",
      "narration": "A React app is a tree of components. One App holds a header, the main content, and a footer, and each of those is its own reusable piece.",
      "durationFrames": 330,
      "timingSource": "estimated",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "transition": "iris",
      "data": {
        "headline": "An app is a [tree.]",
        "headlineColor": "blue",
        "anim": "rise",
        "diagram": {
          "layout": "tree",
          "nodes": [
            {"id": "app", "label": "App", "asset": "lucide:atom", "color": "blue", "atWord": 6},
            {"id": "header", "label": "Header", "asset": "lucide:panel-top", "color": "purple", "atWord": 12, "parent": "app"},
            {"id": "main", "label": "Content", "asset": "lucide:layout", "color": "orange", "atWord": 14, "parent": "app"},
            {"id": "footer", "label": "Footer", "asset": "lucide:panel-bottom", "color": "green", "atWord": 16, "parent": "app"}
          ]
        },
        "source": "A REACT APP: A TREE OF COMPONENTS"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s05",
      "type": "CHAPTER",
      "narration": "Chapter one. Components, the building blocks.",
      "durationFrames": 138,
      "timingSource": "estimated",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "transition": "dip",
      "data": {
        "chapter": {"number": "01", "title": "Components", "subtitle": "the building blocks", "color": "blue"}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s06",
      "type": "CODE_WINDOW",
      "narration": "A component is just a function that returns what the user interface should look like.",
      "durationFrames": 300,
      "timingSource": "estimated",
      "background": "zoneB",
      "transition": "push",
      "data": {
        "code": {
          "filename": "Welcome.jsx",
          "language": "jsx",
          "atWord": 1,
          "lines": [
            {"text": "function Welcome() {"},
            {"text": "  return <h1>Hello!</h1>;"},
            {"text": "}"}
          ],
          "output": [
            {"text": "a component returns UI", "color": "green"}
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s07",
      "type": "CHAPTER",
      "narration": "Chapter two. That HTML-looking syntax has a name: JSX.",
      "durationFrames": 150,
      "timingSource": "estimated",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "transition": "dip",
      "data": {
        "chapter": {"number": "02", "title": "JSX", "subtitle": "markup in JavaScript", "color": "purple"}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s08",
      "type": "CODE_WINDOW",
      "narration": "JSX lets you write markup right inside JavaScript, and drop in any value with curly braces.",
      "durationFrames": 306,
      "timingSource": "estimated",
      "background": "zoneB",
      "transition": "push",
      "data": {
        "code": {
          "filename": "greeting.jsx",
          "language": "jsx",
          "atWord": 1,
          "lines": [
            {"text": "const name = \"Sam\";"},
            {"text": "const el = <h1>Hello, {name}!</h1>;"}
          ],
          "output": [
            {"text": "markup and JavaScript, together", "color": "green"}
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s09",
      "type": "CHAPTER",
      "narration": "Chapter three. Props, passing data in.",
      "durationFrames": 138,
      "timingSource": "estimated",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "transition": "dip",
      "data": {
        "chapter": {"number": "03", "title": "Props", "subtitle": "passing data in", "color": "orange"}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s10",
      "type": "DIAGRAM",
      "narration": "Data flows one way: a parent passes props down to its children, and never back up.",
      "durationFrames": 288,
      "timingSource": "estimated",
      "background": "zoneB",
      "transition": "slide",
      "data": {
        "headline": "Data flows [down.]",
        "headlineColor": "orange",
        "diagram": {
          "layout": "flow",
          "direction": "horizontal",
          "nodes": [
            {"id": "parent", "label": "Parent", "asset": "lucide:box", "color": "blue", "atWord": 6},
            {"id": "child", "label": "Child", "asset": "lucide:box", "color": "purple", "atWord": 9},
            {"id": "grand", "label": "Grandchild", "asset": "lucide:box", "color": "green", "atWord": 11}
          ],
          "edges": [
            {"from": "parent", "to": "child", "label": "props", "atWord": 8, "color": "blue"},
            {"from": "child", "to": "grand", "label": "props", "atWord": 10, "color": "purple"}
          ]
        },
        "source": "ONE-WAY DATA FLOW: PARENT TO CHILD"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s11",
      "type": "CODE_WINDOW",
      "narration": "You pass a prop like an attribute, then read it inside the component through the props object.",
      "durationFrames": 312,
      "timingSource": "estimated",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "transition": "push",
      "data": {
        "code": {
          "filename": "App.jsx",
          "language": "jsx",
          "atWord": 1,
          "lines": [
            {"text": "<Welcome name=\"Sam\" />"},
            {"text": ""},
            {"text": "function Welcome(props) {"},
            {"text": "  return <h1>Hi, {props.name}</h1>;"},
            {"text": "}"}
          ],
          "output": [
            {"text": "props.name is \"Sam\"", "color": "green"}
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s12",
      "type": "CHAPTER",
      "narration": "Chapter four. State, data that changes.",
      "durationFrames": 138,
      "timingSource": "estimated",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "transition": "dip",
      "data": {
        "chapter": {"number": "04", "title": "State", "subtitle": "data that changes", "color": "green"}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s13",
      "type": "CODE_WINDOW",
      "narration": "State is a component's own memory. The useState hook hands you a value and a function to update it.",
      "durationFrames": 330,
      "timingSource": "estimated",
      "background": "zoneB",
      "transition": "push",
      "data": {
        "code": {
          "filename": "Counter.jsx",
          "language": "jsx",
          "atWord": 1,
          "lines": [
            {"text": "const [count, setCount] = useState(0);"},
            {"text": ""},
            {"text": "<button onClick={() => setCount(count + 1)}>"},
            {"text": "  Clicked {count} times"},
            {"text": "</button>"}
          ],
          "output": [
            {"text": "click updates state, UI follows", "color": "green"}
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s14",
      "type": "DIAGRAM",
      "narration": "And here's the magic. When state changes, React re-renders that component and updates what you see on screen.",
      "durationFrames": 300,
      "timingSource": "estimated",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "transition": "iris",
      "data": {
        "headline": "State drives the [screen.]",
        "headlineColor": "green",
        "diagram": {
          "layout": "flow",
          "direction": "horizontal",
          "nodes": [
            {"id": "set", "label": "setState", "asset": "lucide:mouse-pointer-click", "color": "orange", "atWord": 6},
            {"id": "render", "label": "Re-render", "asset": "lucide:refresh-cw", "color": "blue", "atWord": 10},
            {"id": "ui", "label": "Update UI", "asset": "lucide:monitor", "color": "green", "atWord": 13}
          ],
          "edges": [
            {"from": "set", "to": "render", "atWord": 10},
            {"from": "render", "to": "ui", "atWord": 13}
          ]
        },
        "source": "STATE CHANGE TRIGGERS A RE-RENDER"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s15",
      "type": "KINETIC_TEXT",
      "narration": "But React doesn't redraw the whole page. It compares, and updates only what actually changed.",
      "durationFrames": 216,
      "timingSource": "estimated",
      "background": "zoneB",
      "transition": "fade",
      "data": {
        "kinetic": {"fx": "highlight", "text": "It updates only what [changed].", "sub": "fast by design", "color": "blue", "atWord": 8}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s16",
      "type": "REVEAL",
      "narration": "Strip everything away, and React is really just this: components that hold state and describe your UI.",
      "durationFrames": 252,
      "timingSource": "estimated",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "transition": "zoom",
      "fx": "burst",
      "data": {
        "headline": "Components + [state.]",
        "reveal": {"kicker": "THAT'S REACT", "sub": "components hold state and describe the UI", "color": "blue", "atWord": 9}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s17",
      "type": "RECAP",
      "narration": "So that's the core. Components build the UI, JSX describes it, props pass data down, and state makes it interactive.",
      "durationFrames": 342,
      "timingSource": "estimated",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "transition": "iris",
      "data": {
        "heading": "React, recapped",
        "points": [
          {"text": "Components build the UI", "atWord": 5},
          {"text": "JSX describes it", "atWord": 10},
          {"text": "Props pass data down", "atWord": 14},
          {"text": "State makes it interactive", "atWord": 18}
        ]
      }
    },
    {
